    "updated_at": "2020-12-03T11:36:06Z",
    "body": "Yeah, that would work too. The hook could be invoked unconditionally and the appropriate early returns could be on the WebDriver side.\r\n\r\nSo how should this work? It would help to understand what the invariants are when the tree of browsing contexts is modified. Questions:\r\n- Is this in fact a simple tree, or do browsing context groups complicate this?\r\n- Are new browsing contexts always created one at a time, with at least a spin of the event loop between each? Or can some nested `<iframe srcdoc>` or similar situation result in a whole subtree of browsing contexts appearing at once?\r\n- Is removal from the tree of browsing contexts synonymous with [discarding](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/window-object.html#a-browsing-context-is-discarded) that subtree of browsing contexts, or can such browsing contexts somehow be salvaged or revived later?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
