    "created_at": "2020-12-03T12:19:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-12-03T12:19:07Z",
    "body": "A browsing context group is essentially a set of top-level browsing contexts, with some side table. The hierarchy within a top-level browsing context can be considered tree, sorta, if you only look at active documents, but nested browsing contexts are really anchored to documents (and a browsing context is a sequence of those documents).\r\n\r\nThere's also some tracking of insertion order that is not specified well and this matters for name targeting.\r\n\r\nYou can create multiple at the same time by inserting multiple `iframe` elements. Either as children of an element you insert, or together in a `DocumentFragment` that you insert. This is also somewhat poorly specified with regards to the initial about:blank load event these generate and what the state of the world is when that event fires. I did some work on this, but it was hard to get enough attention to the problem to drive it to completion. In any event, the event loop definitely doesn't spin between these.\r\n\r\nSince they are anchored at documents, they might disappear due to navigation and it would depend on the bfcache whether they end up discarded. I think they might end up effectively frozen or some such, but that state isn't really defined. (We probably need to define it, also if we want bfcache to work with COOP.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
